//
// Library.RelocTable.ailang
// OS-agnostic relocation record accumulator.
// Location: Librarys/Compiler/Link/Core/Library.RelocTable.ailang
// Import:   LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.RelocTable
//
// PURPOSE:
//   Collects relocation records during codegen so the output emitter can
//   flush them into the appropriate section at finalize time:
//     - Linux ET_REL .ko   -> .rela.text (Elf64_Rela, 24 bytes each)
//     - Linux ET_EXEC      -> no relocs if direct-syscall; PLT if libc-linked
//     - Haiku / macOS etc. -> their respective dynamic reloc sections
//
// RECORD SHAPE (OS-agnostic):
//   text_offset  : u64   // byte offset into emitted .text where the 4-byte
//                        // displacement placeholder lives (for PLT32: insn_end - 4)
//   sym_name     : s     // symbol name; resolved to sym_idx at flush time
//   reloc_type   : u32   // R_X86_64_PLT32 = 4, R_X86_64_PC32 = 2, etc.
//   addend       : i64   // typically -4 for `call rel32` via E8
//
// STATUS: Scaffold. Storage strategy TBD — FixedPool of structs vs.
// four parallel XArrays. Match whatever CELFBuilder already does so we
// can reuse its serialization idioms.
